 {id:'mda',slug:'people/mda-space-mike-greenley',t:'How Canada’s leading space company plans to build and protect',d:'MDA Space CEO Mike Greenley on space sovereignty, co-operating with the U.S. and protecting Canada from above',img:R('image-8b3cf213a33b58af8224631e830c7ea63d604aed-2880x1920-webp'),p:'People',s:'',tags:['Science & tech'],a:'Lisa Hrabluk',date:'June 11, 2026',m:8,
  body:['Mike Greenley joined MDA Space in 2018 and has served as CEO since 2020, guiding its evolution from a company best known for the Canadarm to one increasingly focused on satellite systems, defence programs and autonomous space technologies. That shift is unfolding as Canada launches a more robust agenda around space sovereignty and Arctic security, and as the country considers its role in U.S.-led defence initiatives.']},
 {id:'arctic',slug:'ideas/arctic-sovereignty-us-canada-summit',t:'Canada’s fight against a global free-for-all in the Arctic',d:'Why experts say Canada’s Arctic sovereignty is already a myth, and what needs to be done',img:R('image-c2ec4e407a119c9e4ea9e9324aa07f7eff82bf17-2000x1333-jpg'),p:'Ideas',s:'',tags:['Economy'],a:'Tim Harper',date:'June 12, 2026',m:4,
  body:['The concept of Canadian Arctic sovereignty is rapidly becoming outdated as much of the world eyes the region as part of an intense global competition that will blur traditional lines and beliefs, a conference on Canada-U.S. relations was told this week.']},
 {id:'spaceport',slug:'places/canada-spaceport-nova-scotia-nordspace',t:'Inside Canada’s race for space sovereignty',d:'Atlantic Canada is launching the country into the final frontier',img:R('image-e5571f84c0db0257ff10b37f655ac837f9dc100a-2160x1260-png'),p:'Places',s:'',tags:['Science & tech'],a:'Lisa Hrabluk',date:'April 2, 2026',m:17,
  body:['To understand Canada’s race to space, it helps to look out to sea.']},
 {id:'cups',slug:'ideas/fifa-world-cup-toronto-muuse-reusable-cups',t:'How reusable cups could help solve the World Cup’s garbage problem',d:'Muuse Canada’s cups in Toronto’s FIFA Fan Festival zone may keep 237,000 pounds of plastic out of landfills',img:R('image-6e867b7016639de26eb7834736cee954afe1d374-2016x1260-jpg'),p:'Ideas',s:'',tags:['Climate'],a:'Richie Assaly',date:'June 4, 2026',m:6,
  body:['Last July, a clean-up crew at Wembley Stadium in London went viral after they were captured sweeping up empty plastic cups following a rowdy Oasis reunion concert, where an estimated 250,000 pints of beer were consumed.']},
 {id:'sewage',slug:'ideas/sewage-heat-recovery-senakw-blatchford-canada',t:'These apartment buildings will be heated by sewage – yes, really',d:'The scale and ingenuity of this Vancouver project is the next step in an energy revolution shaping development across Canada',img:R('image-bef87033b3af50417a6cd1faf885c3c123ed18ad-2160x1260-jpg'),p:'Ideas',s:'',tags:['Housing','Energy'],a:'Stefan Novakovic',date:'May 22, 2026',m:9,
  body:['In downtown Vancouver, it takes a lot for new towers to stand out. Since the turn of the millennium, a landscape of highrise construction cranes has become an enduring complement to the majestic mountains and waterways that frame the city. Yet, even amid the thicket of soaring condominiums and sublime natural surroundings, Sen̓áḵw is a showstopper.']}
